# Per-package USE flags — NVIDIA Jetson Orin (Tegra234, aarch64).
# Mirrors the RPi5/Frite cross-build fixups that are arch- (not board-) specific.

# gentoo-sources: install the source symlink so the kernel build can find it.
sys-kernel/gentoo-sources symlink

# parted needs device-mapper for the installer's partitioning helpers.
sys-block/parted device-mapper

# NetworkManager: keep wifi USE (the devkit has an M.2 radio slot; a USB dongle
# may be present) but the radio is rfkill-blocked + module-blacklisted by
# default (harden_radios in the builder). Drop modemmanager: it drags the
# gobject-introspection chain our global -introspection breaks, and cellular
# modems are absent from this target (same rationale as the Frite).
net-misc/networkmanager wifi -modemmanager

# networkmanager[wifi] (forced above) hard-requires wpa_supplicant[dbus] (NM drives
# it over D-Bus). dbus is not a default USE; pre-seed it or payload resolution
# aborts. Verbatim the same pre-seed specs-rpi5/portage/package.use/rpi5:26 and
# specs-x86/portage/package.use/net:18 already carry — this spec forced the wifi
# USE without it, so NetworkManager could never merge and ALL FOUR Jetson roles
# (edge_ai, full, gpu-host, jetson-desktop) failed the payload assert with zero
# artifacts in the 2026-07-19 sweep:
#     The following USE changes are necessary to proceed:
#     # required by net-misc/networkmanager-1.56.1::gentoo[wifi,-iwd]
#     >=net-wireless/wpa_supplicant-2.11-r5 dbus
net-wireless/wpa_supplicant dbus

# containerd on the hardened/selinux profile (k8s roles): the selinux USE is
# profile-forced; the HOST-side toolchain pre-seed lives in the builder (see the
# rpi5 builder's host package.use note) — this covers the TARGET side.
sys-libs/libselinux python
sys-process/audit python

# freetype needs harfbuzz to satisfy pango for the desktop role's GTK stack
# (transitively also dbus/elogind/dracut). Harmless on headless roles.
media-libs/freetype harfbuzz

# ngtcp2 needs gnutls to satisfy net-fs/samba pulled in by net-fs/cifs-utils[acl].
net-libs/ngtcp2 gnutls

# libdom needs xml to satisfy www-client/netsurf[svgtiny,svg] (desktop role).
net-libs/libdom xml

# gtk+ rsvg USE disabled (desktop role): librsvg is a Rust crate; cross-compiling
# it needs the aarch64 Rust stdlib target absent from the host toolchain. SVG
# icon rendering is non-essential; adwaita is satisfied via profile/package.provided.
x11-libs/gtk+ -rsvg

# libfm automount disabled (desktop role): +automount drags the whole gvfs →
# gcr:4 → gtk-4 chain that fails to cross-compile (same as the Frite).
x11-libs/libfm -automount

# pinentry gtk USE disabled: +gtk requires app-crypt/gcr:4[gtk] → gui-libs/gtk-4
# (fails cross-configure). The curses backend is sufficient on this node.
app-crypt/pinentry -gtk

# xterm: no toolbar bloat (desktop role).
x11-terms/xterm -toolbar
